    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0701" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg631"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Van Limburg.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 7, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In answer to your second note of this date,
                    in which you request the proof upon which Major General Butler based his
                    proceedings against the consul of the Netherlands at New Orleans, I have to
                    inform you, with entire frankness, that my communications to you upon the
                    subject have been drawn from the report of that officer with reference to his
                    proceedings in that city, generally, up to the 16th of last month, the date of
                    the report. That document not being accompanied by any proof of the allegations
                    against the consul, it is quite beyond my power, at this time, to comply with
                    your request.</p>
                <p>I offer to you, sir, a renewed assurance of my very high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roest Van Limburg,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
